{:title "Competitor discovery"
 :doc "Find products that compete with a given product, each with its site, a one-line claim and a quote from a page the run fetched. Scored on recall of a reference set, on grounding (a quote counts only if it is on a page the run fetched) and on relevance (a judge model)."
 :task "Read /docs/product.md: it describes {product}. Find products that compete with {product}: shared workspaces or systems where people and AI agents work together on an organization's state. Search the web with the Brave Search API: (babashka.http-client/get \"https://api.search.brave.com/res/v1/web/search\" {:query-params {:q query :count 10} :headers {\"X-Subscription-Token\" (env/get \"BRAVE_API_KEY\")}}) (the token is a placeholder the sandbox fills in); results are under [:web :results] of the JSON body. Use at most {max-searches} searches. Fetch each candidate's own page before you list it. Write /out/competitors.edn: a vector of maps {:name :url :claim :quote :source-url}, where :url is the product's site, :claim one line on what it does, and :quote a sentence copied verbatim from the page at :source-url, which you fetched. List only products you checked; at most {max-entries}."
 :params {:product "Simmis" :max-searches 8 :max-entries 10
          :description "an organizational control system for work shared by people and AI agents: a durable shared state, separate attempts, controlled adoption"}
 :judge {:model "claude-code-haiku" :max-requests 12}
 ;; the reference set is simm.is's own comparison: not to be read off it
 :blocked-sources ["simm.is"]
 :profile "developer"
 :capture ["/out"]
 :fetched true
 :timeout-ms 900000}
